          "quote": "Effective on the License Option Exercise Closing Date, as between the Parties, AbbVie shall have the sole right, at its expense, to Manufacture (or have Manufactured) and supply the Licensed Compound and Licensed Products for commercial sale in the Territory by AbbVie and its Affiliates and Sublicensees.",
          "rationale": "The Agreement imposes no minimum purchase, volume, requirements or take-or-pay obligation on AbbVie, so it sits at the preferred position. Searches for \"minimum\", take-or-pay, shortfall, purchase/volume commitment, forecast and requirements/sole-source language returned nothing responsive: the only \"minimum\" hits are the insurance limits in Sections 11.6-11.6.1 (p0573-p0577), which are unrelated. AbbVie's payment obligations are event-contingent consideration for the rights granted - a one-time upfront payment (Section 6.1), development and regulatory milestones payable only on achievement of the specified milestone (Section 6.2), and royalties on actual Net Sales - none of which require AbbVie to buy any quantity or to pay for unused volume. On supply, Section 4.5.1 gives AbbVie the sole right to Manufacture (or have Manufactured) and supply Licensed Compounds and Products at its own expense, and Section 4.5.2 entitles AbbVie to a manufacturing technology transfer, so there is no obligation to source from Harpoon. Article 4.2's Commercially Reasonable Efforts commercialization diligence is a separate efforts standard, not a volume or purchase commitment, and is not flagged here. No redline is warranted; the fallback true-up/reduction mechanics are unnecessary because no commitment exists to reduce.",
